---
fmContentType: glossaryEntry
term: "Sublingual"
letter: "S"
anchor: "sublingual"
category: "edibles"
---

Administration of a substance under the tongue, where it's absorbed directly through the mucous membranes into the bloodstream — bypassing the digestive system and liver. Sublingual cannabis consumption (typically via tincture) produces faster onset than edibles (15–45 minutes vs. 30–120 minutes), shorter duration (2–4 hours vs. 4–8 hours), and a more THC-like effect profile rather than the 11-hydroxy-THC-dominant experience of digested edibles.

→ [How to Make Cannabis Tincture](/edibles/how-to-make-cannabis-tincture-green-golden-dragon/)
